    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148">

                <pb facs="0403" n="393" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg393"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 878.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 21, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Mr. Dudley, our consul at Liverpool, has
                    made a report to this department upon the delays of the proceedings, on our
                    requisition, in the case of the pirate Joseph L. Gerity. I trust that you are
                    doing what can be done to secure a surrender of the offenders.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
